"# JSON and JavaScript Objects\n",
"\n",
"## All About Game Character Objects and JSON\n",
"\n",
"JSON and JavaScript objects are useful ways to organize related information. In game development, they can represent a character's name, level, class, health, skills, inventory, and other game data."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "d14f8a23",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"# 1. LxD Cycle Process\n",
"\n",
"**Empathize:**  \n",
"Beginners often confuse JavaScript objects with JSON because the two look very similar. Students may forget that JSON has stricter rules than JavaScript objects, such as requiring double quotes around keys and not allowing functions, comments, or trailing commas. Students may also have difficulty understanding why JSON is useful outside of JavaScript itself.\n",
"\n",
"**Define:**\n",
"\n",
"**POV:**  \n",
"JavaScript students need to understand the difference between JavaScript objects and JSON because both use key-value structures, but JSON follows stricter rules and is primarily used to store and transfer data.\n",
"\n",
"**Learning Goal:**  \n",
"Students will create JavaScript objects, access object properties, understand JSON syntax rules, convert JavaScript objects to JSON strings, and parse JSON strings back into JavaScript objects.\n",
"\n",
"**Ideate:**\n",
"\n",
"**HMW Question:**  \n",
"How might we help students recognize the difference between a JavaScript object and JSON?\n",
"\n",
"**HMW Question:**  \n",
"How might we make JSON useful and understandable by connecting it to something familiar, such as a game character profile?\n",
"\n",
"**Activity:**  \n",
"Students create and personalize a game-character object, access properties using dot notation, identify valid and invalid JSON, convert JavaScript objects into JSON strings, parse JSON strings back into JavaScript objects, and build a personalized character sheet using nested objects and arrays.\n",
"\n",
"**Prototype & Test:**  \n",
"Lesson authors: Add what happened during the trial run and what students found difficult. Record any changes made to the examples, instructions, or activities."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "e39b61c7",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"# 2. Lesson Plan\n",
"\n",
"**Learning Objective:**  \n",
"Students will understand how JavaScript objects store key-value data and how JSON is used to store and transfer structured data.\n",
"\n",
"**Success Criteria:**  \n",
"You can create a JavaScript object, access properties using dot notation, explain the difference between JavaScript objects and JSON, identify JSON syntax rules, use JSON.stringify(), use JSON.parse(), and create nested objects containing arrays."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "f21d73b4",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Tech Talk: Objects and JSON\n",
"\n",
"A JavaScript object stores related information using key-value pairs.\n",
"\n",
"For example, a game character can store a name, level, and class in one object.\n",
"\n",
"JSON stands for **JavaScript Object Notation**. Even though JavaScript is in the name, JSON is not JavaScript code. JSON is a text format used to store and transfer data.\n",
"\n",
"JSON has stricter rules than JavaScript objects:\n",
"\n",
"- Keys require double quotes.\n",
"- Strings require double quotes.\n",
"- Functions are not allowed.\n",
"- Comments are not allowed.\n",
"- Trailing commas are not allowed.\n",
"\n",
"JavaScript provides two important methods for working with JSON:\n",
"\n",
"- **JSON.stringify()** converts a JavaScript object into a JSON string.\n",
"- **JSON.parse()** converts a JSON string into a JavaScript object."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "b6e42a91",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"# 3. Reference Guide\n",
"\n",
"## Key Vocabulary\n",
"\n",
"| Term | Definition | Example |\n",
"|---|---|---|\n",
"| Object | A JavaScript structure containing key-value pairs | `{name: \"Steve\"}` |\n",
"| Key | The name of a property | `name` |\n",
"| Value | The information stored under a key | `\"Steve\"` |\n",
"| Property | A key-value pair in an object | `name: \"Steve\"` |\n",
"| Nested Object | An object stored inside another object | `character_info: {level: 10}` |\n",
"| Array | An ordered list of values | `skills: [\"Attack\", \"Heal\"]` |\n",
"| JSON | A text format used to store and transfer structured data | `{\"name\":\"Steve\"}` |\n",
"| JSON.stringify() | Converts an object into a JSON string | `JSON.stringify(user)` |\n",
"| JSON.parse() | Converts JSON into a JavaScript object | `JSON.parse(jsonString)` |\n",
"| Undefined | The value returned when a property does not exist | `character.element` |"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "91a5cd62",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## JavaScript Objects vs. JSON\n",
"\n",
"| Feature | JavaScript Object | JSON |\n",
"|---|---|---|\n",
"| Keys | Quotes optional | Double quotes required |\n",
"| Functions | Allowed | Not allowed |\n",
"| Comments | Allowed in JavaScript | Not allowed |\n",
"| Trailing commas | Can be allowed | Not allowed |\n",
"| Purpose | Used directly in JavaScript | Store and transfer data as text |\n",
"| Conversion | `JSON.stringify()` | `JSON.parse()` |"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
