"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Code Example 2: JSON Rules\n",
"\n",
"Valid JSON requires double quotes around keys and strings."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"id": "42d8f6ac",
"metadata": {
"vscode": {
"languageId": "javascript"
}
},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"%%js\n",
"\n",
"// CODE_RUNNER: Parse valid JSON.\n",
"\n",
"const jsonData = `\n",
    "{\n",
    "    \"name\": \"Steve\",\n",
    "    \"level\": 10,\n",
    "    \"class\": \"Warrior\",\n",
    "    \"online\": true\n",
    "}\n",
    "`;\n",
"\n",
"const parsedData = JSON.parse(jsonData);\n",
"\n",
"console.log(parsedData);\n",
"console.log("Name:", parsedData.name);\n",
"console.log("Level:", parsedData.level);"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "8a31de95",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"Try intentionally breaking the JSON.\n",
"\n",
"- Remove quotes from a key.\n",
"- Add a trailing comma.\n",
"- Change `true` to `True`.\n",
"- Add a comment.\n",
"\n",
"Run the code after each change and observe the error."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "f57c21b8",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Code Example 3: JSON.stringify() and JSON.parse()\n",
"\n",
"`JSON.stringify()` converts a JavaScript object into a JSON string. `JSON.parse()` converts that JSON string back into a JavaScript object."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"id": "63e9ab17",
"metadata": {
"vscode": {
"languageId": "javascript"
}
},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"%%js\n",
"\n",
"// CODE_RUNNER: Convert an object to JSON and back.\n",
"\n",
"const user = {\n",
"    username: "PLAYER_1",\n",
"    password: 12345,\n",
"    isOnline: false\n",
"};\n",
"\n",
"const jsonString = JSON.stringify(user);\n",
"\n",
"console.log("JSON string:");\n",
"console.log(jsonString);\n",
"\n",
"const parsedUser = JSON.parse(jsonString);\n",
"\n",
"console.log("JavaScript object:");\n",
"console.log(parsedUser);"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"id": "b49d7e26",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## Code Example 4: Nested Objects and Arrays\n",
"\n",
"Objects can contain other objects and arrays. This is useful for organizing more complex game data."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"id": "e82c14f5",
"metadata": {
"vscode": {
"languageId": "javascript"
}
},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"%%js\n",
"\n",
"// CODE_RUNNER: Create a nested character object.\n",
"\n",
"const character = {\n",
"    name: "Steve",\n",
"    username: "PLAYER_1",\n",
"    character_info: {\n",
"        level: 10,\n",
"        class: "Warrior",\n",
"        health: 100\n",
"    },\n",
"    skills: ["Attack", "Defend", "Heal"]\n",
"};\n",
"\n",
"console.log("Name:", character.name);\n",
"console.log("Username:", character.username);\n",
"console.log("Level:", character.character_info.level);\n",
"console.log("Class:", character.character_info.class);\n",
"console.log("Health:", character.character_info.health);\n",
"console.log("Skills:", character.skills);"
]
},
